VALUES (586, 'J1', $t$ASK 586 J1: a result against the defender needs the keystone broken (both seatings), with the keystone reader fix$t$,
  $t$A judge's RESULT against the defender requires the judge's own KEYSTONE line to read BROKEN; a BROKEN verdict beside a keystone that STANDS gives UNDERDETERMINED, in both seatings. (The operator's press "Keystone must break", ruling row 510; plan ask586/w3/plan586.md rev 6, J1; card586j1.md.)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 on the operator's press "Write J1" at 01:58 CST 2026-11-24, with no debate run live, on top of the ASK 595 write (Wall 11483; audit 41330). Engine moMxiV4Irg1uRBZN 6e0c5013 to 0714bdd9-cc73-4caa-bcc1-a2b115d26906; changed: Panel Build, Build Independent Verdict, Shared Library (library lines 1286, 1351, 1492). Child MqQHRl7mQQ0z8QdT e7f13f7e to be711308-fcd5-4515-927d-9e68049a6899. LIB 15b919ff55fc0fd7, MAP ff6050a03e645ec4. THIS REVERSES A WRITTEN RULE, and the card said so: engine manual part 08.0 let a BROKEN verdict give CHALLENGER WINS while the judge's KEYSTONE line read STANDS. What is live (card586j1.md section 2): (1) the judges' text in Panel Build gains: "A RESULT against the defender requires your KEYSTONE line to read BROKEN, by a collision line on the keystone link or by the link it rests on. If your keystone line reads STANDS, you may not write a RESULT against the defender: write UNDERDETERMINED unless your verdict is HELD." (2) The seat's word: a BROKEN verdict with the keystone STANDS gives UNDERDETERMINED; the break stays on its line and counts as a broken link. (3) The engine gives the seat's word by the same rule in the three places it computes it (the recompute, the audit tag, the gate after the send-back), and the record names the rule when it moves the word. (4) R1: the keystone reader also reads the form "KEYSTONE: D5 vs C2 (Numbers 1:2, Hebrews 2:16) -- STANDS". (5) Both seatings. Build Independent Verdict carries the same text and does not run (Wall 11462, 11467). What it would have changed in stored runs (nothing stored is rewritten): Oracle as challenger, 171 runs and 513 judgments of 2026-10-02 to 11-17, 149 judgments CHALLENGER WINS, of them 56 in 32 runs beside KEYSTONE STANDS (W4, Wall 11461); W1's own SQL finds 53 with a stricter RESULT parse and the same 32 runs (Wall 11467). Oracle as defender, runs 41418, 41822, 42071: 3 of 9 judgments (1271, 1272, 1273); run 41822 was stored CHALLENGER PREVAILS 2 to 1 and one of its two votes is 1271. The path: ruling 510 (23:14 CST 11-23); the build deba0391; the re-cut on the live base and the replay (Wall 11461); W1 PASS with R1 (Wall 11467); R1 built (Wall 11470); the card; the press; the write (Wall 11483); W1 readback MATCH (Wall 11485). IN PART, for two reasons. (1) No run has executed on 0714bdd9 or a later version; the first live run is the first test of the judges' new sentence. (2) THE R1 READER WAS BUILT AFTER THE GRADE. W1's grade (Wall 11467) covers the build deba0391 re-cut on both bases and ACCEPTS R1 as a proposal, naming three tests; W4 built R1 and ran four tests (Wall 11470) and carded it. The Wall posts W3 read hold no grade by W1 of the R1 code as built before the write. W1's readback (Wall 11485) reports that the written version differs from W1's own rebuild only at library line 1286, describes the reader as written, and gives MATCH to W4's target. W1 confirmed after the write that this stands as its grade of R1 as built, and ran t_r1 on the written engine, 4 PASS (Wall 11498). So the R1 code went live before a grader had run it.$t$,
  '11461, 11467, 11470, 11483, 11485, 11498',
  current_setting('truth.session_id'), NULL,
  to_jsonb($t$23:14 CST 2026-11-23, press "Keystone must break" on the coordinator's card in the project chat (ruling row 510; the press itself was not seen by W3). "Rule live now", 23:30 CST 2026-11-23, as card586j1.md gives it (no md_notes_rulings row of seat 33 holds it). His press at 01:58 CST 2026-11-24 in W4's thread: "Write J1" (as Wall 11483 gives it).$t$::text),
  $j${"answer": "Write J1", "source": "Wall 11483; audit 41330", "thread": "W4", "press_time": "01:58 CST 2026-11-24", "question": "not in the record W3 read (the card is in W4's thread); the card text is ask586/w4/j1write/card586j1.md bdd0ee7a"}$j$::jsonb,
  'W4',
  $j${"md5": "7b81e80d", "path": "ask586/w3/plan586.md", "commit": "not read by W3 for this row", "note": "W3's plan rev 6, J1 both seatings (W1 PASS with C6 and C7, Wall 11381)", "source": "md5sum by W3; card586j1.md"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"md5": "591be87d", "path": "ask586/w4/j1recut_fix595/target_engine_586j1.json", "note": "the engine target on the ASK 595 base, with the R1 reader; written and read back", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11470, 11485"}, {"md5": "f5db5a46", "path": "ask586/w4/j1recut_fix595/target_child_586j1.json", "note": "the child target on the ASK 595 base, with R1", "source": "md5sum by W3; Wall 11470, 11485"}, {"md5": "be629524", "path": "ask586/w4/j1recut_live/target_engine_586j1.json", "note": "the engine target on base d819ff4c, with R1; not written", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "7f37d2e6", "path": "ask586/w4/j1recut_live/target_child_586j1.json", "note": "the child target on base 31329164, with R1; not written", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "723f080d", "path": "ask586/w4/j1recut_fix595/build586j1.cjs", "note": "the build script", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "3ce40f95", "path": "ask586/w4/j1recut_fix595/t586j1.cjs", "note": "the test, 31 cases", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "4745ffeb", "path": "ask586/w4/j1recut_fix595/t_r1.cjs", "note": "the R1 reader test, 4 cases", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "57119af0", "path": "ask586/w4/j1write/t586j1_at_write.txt", "note": "test output at the write; the same md5 as j1recut_fix595/out_t586j1.txt", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "e793e158", "path": "ask586/w4/j1write/t_r1_at_write.txt", "note": "R1 test output at the write; the same md5 as j1recut_fix595/out_t_r1.txt", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "09319c78", "path": "ask586/w4/j1recut_fix595/b3replay.cjs", "note": "the replay script", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "bdd0ee7a", "path": "ask586/w4/j1write/card586j1.md", "note": "the card text", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "1987f2eb", "path": "ask586/w4/j1write/prewrite_eng586j1.json", "note": "fresh fetch before the write; the same md5 as ASK 595's fetch-back", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "2dabe69f", "path": "ask586/w4/j1write/prewrite_child586j1.json", "note": "fresh fetch before the write, child", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "a8b21cb6", "path": "ask586/w4/j1write/put_eng586j1.json", "note": "PUT body, engine", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "4c72fd06", "path": "ask586/w4/j1write/put_child586j1.json", "note": "PUT body, child", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "d4d7c074", "path": "ask586/w4/j1write/fetchback_eng586j1.json", "note": "fetch-back after the write", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "da70f880", "path": "ask586/w4/j1write/fetchback_child586j1.json", "note": "fetch-back after the write, child", "source": "md5sum by W3"}, {"md5": "7f3697e8", "path": "ask586/w4/j1write/write586j1.sh", "note": "the write script", "source": "md5sum by W3"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"copy": "restore the engine and the child together from ask586/w4/j1write/revert_eng586j1.json 7ccf5572 and revert_child586j1.json 5f0f8864 (to 6e0c5013 and e7f13f7e). A revert now would also undo 586 J6, written on top.", "path": "ask586/w4/j1write/revert_eng586j1.json; ask586/w4/j1write/revert_child586j1.json", "source": "audit 41330; md5sum by W3 (the two files have the md5s of ASK 595's PUT bodies); the last sentence is W3's reading of the chain in Wall 11485"}$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "verdict": "PASS with R1 (the build deba0391 re-cut on d819ff4c/31329164 and on the 595 targets, BEFORE the R1 reader: W1's rebuild equals both of W4's target pairs, 0 differences; t586j1 ALL PASS on both; the replay confirmed by W1's own SQL; R1 the reader fix ACCEPTED, with three tests named)", "wall_id": 11467, "md5_graded": "not in the record: the targets W1 graded were rebuilt with R1 afterwards (Wall 11470) and their md5s are not on the Wall", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11467"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "READBACK MATCH of the written version to W4's target j1recut_fix595; against W1's own rebuild only library line 1286 differs, \"which is the R1 reader added after it\", and W1 describes the reader as written. CONFIRMED by W1 as its grade of R1 as built (Wall 11498): the written 0714bdd9 differs from W1's graded rebuild only at library line 1286, by the change W1 proposed; W1 ran t_r1 on the written engine, 4 PASS. That confirmation and that run came AFTER THE WRITE.", "wall_id": 11485, "md5_graded": "591be87d", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11485 item 2 and Wall 11498 item A; the md5 is md5sum by W3 on ask586/w4/j1recut_fix595/target_engine_586j1.json"}, {"seat": "W1", "verdict": "the same, the child target; CONFIRMED by W1 after the write (Wall 11498)", "wall_id": 11485, "md5_graded": "f5db5a46", "verdict_norm": "PASS", "source": "Wall 11485 item 2 and Wall 11498 item A; md5sum by W3 on ask586/w4/j1recut_fix595/target_child_586j1.json"}]$j$::jsonb,
  ARRAY['591be87d','f5db5a46'], '[41330]'::jsonb,
  $j$[{"kind": "n8n workflow", "name": "ORACLE_DEBATE_V1 moMxiV4Irg1uRBZN", "before": "6e0c5013", "after": "0714bdd9-cc73-4caa-bcc1-a2b115d26906"}, {"kind": "n8n workflow", "name": "child MqQHRl7mQQ0z8QdT", "before": "e7f13f7e", "after": "be711308-fcd5-4515-927d-9e68049a6899"}, {"kind": "n8n nodes, changed", "name": "engine: Panel Build, Build Independent Verdict, Shared Library (library lines 1286, 1351, 1492); child: Shared Library", "before": "as in 6e0c5013 and e7f13f7e", "after": "as in the targets (Wall 11483 item 2; 11485 item 2)"}, {"kind": "library", "name": "Shared Library, engine and child", "before": "LIB 0e45d9fe625d140d, MAP ccda7f6937ff007a", "after": "LIB 15b919ff55fc0fd7, MAP ff6050a03e645ec4"}, {"kind": "rule", "name": "engine manual part 08.0, the RESULT rule", "before": "BROKEN gives CHALLENGER WINS when its standing conditions hold, whatever the KEYSTONE line reads", "after": "CHALLENGER WINS also needs the KEYSTONE line BROKEN; the manual text is not yet written (see manuals)"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"name": "t586j1.cjs, 31 cases", "result": "31 PASS on each base and at the write", "source": "Wall 11461 item 1; 11467; 11470; 11483 item 2"}, {"name": "t_r1.cjs, 4 cases (the keystone reader)", "result": "4 PASS on each base and at the write: judgment 1221's form reads STANDS; the same form with BROKEN reads BROKEN; \"-- STANDS -- GROUND:\" takes no later word; the old form still reads. Run by W4 before the write; rerun by W1 on the written engine after the write, 4 PASS (Wall 11498)", "source": "Wall 11470; 11483 item 2; 11498"}, {"name": "Library Check pair", "result": "PASSES: LIB 15b919ff55fc0fd7, MAP ff6050a03e645ec4", "source": "Wall 11485 item 2"}, {"name": "Replay on stored judgments, Oracle as challenger", "result": "171 runs, 513 judgments: 149 CHALLENGER WINS, 56 beside KEYSTONE STANDS in 32 runs (W4); 53 in the same 32 runs by W1's parse. Not counted by W4: 3 judgments with no KEYSTONE line, 9 with no readable keystone word, 5 with no RESULT line", "source": "Wall 11461 items 2 and 4; 11467"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j$[{"seat": "W1", "wall_id": 11485, "result": "MATCH (fresh fetch from n8n history: 0714bdd9 and be711308, 0 differences to j1recut_fix595; against W1's rebuild only library line 1286, the R1 reader; from 595: Panel Build, Build Independent Verdict, Shared Library lines 1286, 1351, 1492; Library Check PASS)"}]$j$::jsonb,
  $j${"case": "UNEXERCISED. No run has executed on 0714bdd9 or a later version (debate_results last row 03:57 UTC 2026-11-24; Wall 11485). EXPECT on the first run in which a judge writes a BROKEN verdict beside KEYSTONE STANDS: that seat's word is UNDERDETERMINED and the record names the rule; no judgment holds RESULT CHALLENGER WINS beside KEYSTONE STANDS, or, if a judge writes one, the engine moves the seat's word.", "source": "card586j1.md section 2; the EXPECT is W3's reading"}$j$::jsonb,
